  "findings": [
    "Original range-cache-only matrix keeps two concurrent HTTP reads and four warm discovery requests with 16 MiB range cache.",
    "Factory caching adds decoded/raw/discovery competition. At 64 MiB pool and 16 MiB cache setting, cold/warm requests are 41/12; at 128 MiB, 37/0.",
    "No additional failed or budget-rejected jobs in either matrix.",
    "Post-measurement reclamation validates zero final reservations; its artificial reservation peak is excluded from recorded rounds."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One run per scenario; latency and fairness claims require repeated measurements.",
    "Node samples include server and fixture storage and are not Worker heap evidence.",
    "The factory mode combines multiple caches, so its cacheMiB setting is not a combined total-cache cap. The shared pool bounds their combined tracked allocations.",
    "Remaining allocation gaps and full acceptance review stay open."
  ]
